claim.claim-text:
1. A hollow-structured cooling fan, comprising:
a fan frame, wherein a cylindrical mounting tube is disposed in a central portion of the fan frame, and a first bearing is disposed within the mounting tube;
a fan assembly, wherein a hollow sleeve shaft is disposed in a central portion of the fan assembly, the sleeve shaft is inserted into the mounting tube, an outer wall of the sleeve shaft is connected to an inner ring of the first bearing, and a second bearing is disposed within the sleeve shaft;
a display module, wherein a hollow fixed shaft is disposed in a central portion of the display module, the fixed shaft is inserted into the sleeve shaft, and an outer wall of the fixed shaft is connected to an inner ring of the second bearing; and an end portion of an insertion end of the fixed shaft extends through a bottom of the mounting tube to form a limiting connection; and
a drive module, wherein the drive module is disposed on an outer side of the mounting tube and cooperates with the fan assembly; and when the drive module drives the fan assembly to rotate, the display module is in a stationary state through the fixed shaft.
